.Dd September 22, 2026
.Dt MOP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mop
.Nd access encrypted CloudKit secrets using the Mac Secure Enclave
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
stores independently encrypted secrets in a private CloudKit database.
Each named vault has a stable UUID and a custom record zone.
Every command accessing secrets authenticates afresh with Touch ID or the
system password. Strict biometric device keys have no password fallback.
Private keys remain in the local Secure Enclave and nonsynchronizing Keychain.
CloudKit receives ciphertext, discoverable vault names, and public device metadata.
.Pp
Requires macOS 15 or later, Secure Enclave hardware, an available user session,
and a provisioned signed application with matching Keychain and CloudKit entitlements.
.Sh VAULT SELECTION
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -vault Ar NAME-OR-UUID
Constrain reference commands to this vault. References select their own named vault;
management commands otherwise use the account-scoped saved default.
.It Fl -state-directory Ar PATH
Local metadata/cache directory. Defaults to MOP_STATE_DIRECTORY or ~/.mop.
Never synchronize this directory.
.It Fl -offline
Use the last authenticated encrypted cache for read, list, run, inject, or export.
Local authentication is still required. Cache age is printed to stderr.
Remote revocation cannot be checked. Offline mutations are rejected.
.El
.Pp
Normal commands fetch current cloud state. There is no automatic offline fallback.
Legacy vault formats are unsupported; no migration is provided.
.Sh SECRET COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm read Ar REFERENCE
Read a UTF-8 secret, followed by a newline unless -n is supplied.
OTP fields return the generated value for the current time, never the stored seed or provisioning URL.
.It Cm write Op Fl -replace Ar REFERENCE
Read a secret from hidden terminal input or UTF-8 stdin. Never provide a secret
as a command argument. Ordinary writes refuse existing fields; --replace requires one.
.It Cm list Op Fl -vault Ar NAME Op Fl -json
List references without values across all enrolled named vaults using one authentication
per command, or select one by
name or UUID. An included vault failure produces no partial output.
.It Cm delete Ar REFERENCE
Delete a field after authentication and server confirmation.
.It Cm run Op Fl -env-file Ar FILE Op Fl -no-masking Fl - Ar COMMAND Op Ar ARGS
Resolve environment references and execute directly, without an implicit shell.
Dotenv files are literal; later files override inherited and earlier variables.
Exact nonempty fetched secrets are masked on stdout/stderr unless --no-masking is set.
.It Cm inject Op Fl i Ar FILE
Resolve {{ mop://... }} template placeholders from stdin or a UTF-8 file.
.El
.Pp
References use mop://vault/item/[section/]field. Vault names contain 1-63 lowercase
letters/digits separated by single hyphens; other components are percent-encoded.
Run and inject may resolve references from several vaults.
$NAME and ${NAME} expand reference components from the environment.
Fetched values are never expanded recursively. Commands without secret references
require neither cloud access nor authentication.
.Pp
Read and inject support -o/--out-file, -f/--force, and --file-mode OCTAL.
Output is atomic after all references resolve, defaults to mode 0600, and cannot
target the local state directory. Existing files require --force.
.Sh VAULT COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm vault init Ar NAME Fl -recovery-file Ar PATH Op Fl -device-name Ar NAME Op Fl -strict-biometrics
Create a CloudKit vault and an exclusive offline recovery file. Prints the UUID
and fingerprints. Retain any recovery file after an interrupted initialization.
.It Cm vault list Op Fl -json
Discover vault names, UUIDs, enrollment, and format without unlocking.
.It Cm vault rename Ar NAME-OR-UUID Ar NEW-NAME
Authenticate and rename a vault without changing its UUID or records. Update
existing references; no old-name alias is retained.
.It Cm vault delete Ar NAME-OR-UUID Op Fl -yes
Permanently delete the cloud vault, history, and this Mac's vault cache/trust.
Type the name (UUID for legacy vaults) to confirm. Without a terminal, --yes is
required; fresh local authentication is still required. UUID selection supports
legacy or unreadable vaults without decrypting them. Backups, shared device keys,
and caches on other Macs remain. Offline deletion is rejected. Retry uncertain
results with the same UUID; local cleanup happens only after confirmed absence.
.It Cm vault use Ar NAME-OR-UUID
Set the account-scoped default for management commands only.
.It Cm vault sync
Fetch ciphertext and reconcile interrupted commits without unlocking secrets.
.It Cm vault status
Show cached revision, fetch time, and pending commit status.
.It Cm vault import Fl -file Ar PATH
Verify/import a v4 encrypted backup into an absent cloud head. Preserves UUID,
recovery relationships, and the source file. --fingerprint or --revision can
establish trust using independent evidence. --recovery-file enrolls a replacement
Mac before importing if no enrolled device remains.
.It Cm vault export Fl -out-file Ar PATH Op Fl -force Op Fl -offline
Write a verified encrypted v4 backup. Does not export the recovery private key.
.It Cm vault trust Fl -fingerprint Ar HASH
Pin independently verified vault key identity. Alternatively use --revision HASH
from a known-good backup. Never derive trust evidence solely from cloud data.
.It Cm vault fingerprint
Display the vault fingerprint after authentication and trust verification.
.It Cm vault conflicts
List committed encrypted revision hashes, newest first.
.It Cm vault resolve Fl -revision Ar HASH
Restore historical contents under the current vault name, keys, and device authorization.
.It Cm vault recover Fl -recovery-file Ar PATH
Enroll the current Mac using offline recovery and local authentication.
Accepts --name, --strict-biometrics, and independent --fingerprint/--revision evidence.
.El
.Sh DEVICE COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm device identity
Verify application signing and display its private Keychain group without prompting.
.It Cm device request Op Fl -name Ar NAME Op Fl -strict-biometrics
Create/unlock the local key and publish a public enrollment request. Prints its
request ID and fingerprint.
.It Cm device requests
List public requests, which are not independent trust evidence.
.It Cm device add Ar REQUEST_ID Fl -fingerprint Ar HASH
Approve after comparing the fingerprint through an independent trusted channel.
.It Cm device list
List enrolled device names and fingerprints after authentication.
.It Cm device remove Ar FINGERPRINT
Remove another device and rotate all encryption keys. Remaining Macs must
independently verify the new vault fingerprint. Historical ciphertext and cached
secrets remain decryptable by their former recipients.
.El
.Sh CONCURRENCY AND RECOVERY
A conditional CloudKit head save publishes immutable encrypted records and a
manifest. A stale writer fails rather than overwriting another revision.
Retry conflicts explicitly. Exit 22 indicates an uncertain commit: run vault sync
to reconcile before another write. Mutations are never automatically replayed.
Missing zones are not silently recreated. Old revisions and abandoned staging
records are retained and consume iCloud quota.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa ~/.mop/device.json
Public local device metadata and Keychain account UUID.
.It Pa ~/.mop/cloud/
Account/container/environment/vault-scoped ciphertext cache, journals, and trust.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It 2
Invalid arguments, legacy file configuration, or unsupported offline mutation.
.It 3
Authentication failure.
.It 4
Missing secret.
.It 5
Duplicate secret/vault or existing output.
.It 6 / 8
Keychain failure / invalid signed identity or provisioning.
.It 7 / 15
I/O failure / unsafe file or protected output path.
.It 9 / 10 / 11
Missing vault/default / invalid vault / concurrent write conflict.
.It 12 / 13 / 14 / 16
Unavailable enclave / unenrolled device / invalid device or recovery / untrusted vault.
.It 17 / 18 / 19 / 20 / 21 / 22
Cloud unavailable / account unavailable / quota / throttling / permission / uncertain commit.
.It 23 / 24 / 25 / 26
Invalid vault name / ambiguous name / selection mismatch / unsupported legacy format.
.It 27 / 28
Unconfirmed vault deletion / confirmed cloud deletion with incomplete local cleanup.
.It 29
CloudKit rejected the request configuration; verify record types and query indexes.
.It 126 / 127
Cannot launch command / executable missing.
.El
.Pp
Otherwise child exit status or termination signal is propagated.
.Sh SECURITY
Recovery credentials are a full alternate decryption capability; store offline.
Local decrypted keys and values enter process memory. Masking cannot hide
transformed secrets or deliberate child-process bypasses. Freshness is limited by
observed state; offline reads cannot detect remote revocation or unseen account changes.
CloudKit sharing with other Apple Accounts is not implemented in this version.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Nm mop Cm --help
.Pp
README.md, docs/CLOUDKIT.md, and docs/VALIDATION.md in the source distribution.
